  "body": "When I try to install synapse on Ubuntu 16.04 Xenial i386, there is one missing dependency:\r\n```\r\n$ sudo apt install matrix-synapse\r\nReading package lists... Done\r\nBuilding dependency tree       \r\nReading state information... Done\r\nSome packages could not be installed. This may mean that you have\r\nrequested an impossible situation or if you are using the unstable\r\ndistribution that some required packages have not yet been created\r\nor been moved out of Incoming.\r\nThe following information may help to resolve the situation:\r\n\r\nThe following packages have unmet dependencies:\r\n matrix-synapse : Depends: python-ujson but it is not installable\r\nE: Unable to correct problems, you have held broken packages.\r\n```\r\nAnd indeed, the python-ujson package for Xenial seems absent from https://matrix.org/packages/debian/pool/main/u/ujson/. Maybe because this package is included in the official repo of Ubuntu since Xenial. But it's apparently only available for amd64 architecture as indicated on this page: https://packages.ubuntu.com/fr/xenial/python-ujson. The Matrix repo should therefore provides python-ujson for i386 architecture on Xenial.",
